From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: winex11: a window no window manager manages asks for focus at CurrentTime

David: switch programs with the taskbar and "sometimes the input does not
work" (Firefox, Notepad). The activated window asked X for the keyboard with
a time made from its thread's last message; the taskbar click that had just
moved X focus carried a later time (under Xwayland input times come from the
compositor's clock), so the server ignored the request. Wine believed the
window had the focus while X kept the keyboard elsewhere. ICCCM's
last-event-time rule is for managed windows, where a window manager
arbitrates; the shell desktop's windows are not managed.

Gate: make test-focusactivate (the race made certain: the activated window is
held while X focus moves later, then must still get the keyboard).
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -619,7 +619,18 @@
 
     if (!data->whole_window) return;
 
-    if (EVENT_x11_time_to_win32_time(0))
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a window no window manager manages (the shell desktop's
+     * windows, activated by the taskbar from explorer's process) asks with
+     * CurrentTime. The time made from this thread's last message was older
+     * than the taskbar click that had just given X focus to the desktop -- under
+     * Xwayland input times come from the compositor's clock -- and the server
+     * ignored the request: Wine said the window had the focus, the keyboard
+     * stayed on the desktop (David: after switching with the taskbar,
+     * "sometimes the input does not work"). ICCCM's rule is for managed
+     * windows, where a window manager arbitrates. */
+    if (!data->managed)
+        timestamp = CurrentTime;
+    else if (EVENT_x11_time_to_win32_time(0))
         /* ICCCM says don't use CurrentTime, so try to use last message time if possible */
         /* FIXME: this is not entirely correct */
         timestamp = NtUserGetThreadInfo()->message_time - EVENT_x11_time_to_win32_time(0);
